{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LocalUniformLimitEntire","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdMeromorphic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.NormedSpace.MultipliableUniformlyOn"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.phiBProd_meromorphicOn_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.phiBProd_meromorphicOn_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L185-L189","doc":"**`phiBProd` is meromorphic at the physical substrate b-map** (`t = ln q₀ > 0`), with no\nanalytic hypothesis remaining — the substrate branch satisfies `Im b² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.phiBProd_meromorphicOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.phiBProd_meromorphicOn","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L176-L183","doc":"**`phiBProd b` is meromorphic on `ℂ` — unconditionally, on the branch `Im b² > 0`.**\nInput 1 of the Faddeev keystone is now closed with no remaining analytic hypothesis: the two\nproducts are entire (local-uniform limits of entire partial products) and their quotient is\nmeromorphic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.analyticOnNhd_den_tprod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.analyticOnNhd_den_tprod","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L170-L174","doc":"**The denominator infinite product is entire** on the branch `Im b² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.analyticOnNhd_num_tprod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.analyticOnNhd_num_tprod","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L164-L168","doc":"**The numerator infinite product is entire** on the branch `Im b² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_denFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_denFactor","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L123-L160","doc":"**Denominator partial products converge locally uniformly** (branch `Im b² > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_numFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_numFactor","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L87-L121","doc":"**Numerator partial products converge locally uniformly** (branch `Im b² > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_prod_one_add_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence.tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_prod_one_add_exp","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdProductConvergence.lean#L48-L83","doc":"**Local-uniform convergence of `∏(1 + exp(affine + k·c))` for `Re c < 0`.** The generic\nengine: for any continuous `E : ℂ → ℂ` and constant `c` with `Re c < 0`, the `Finset.range`\npartial products of `1 + exp(E z + k c)` converge locally uniformly on `ℂ` to the `tprod`.\nOn each compact `K` the factor norms are dominated by the summable geometric\n`e^{M_K}·(e^{Re c})^k`; `hasProdLocallyUniformlyOn_of_forall_compact` glues the compacts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}